/-! # Pullback of scalar Ext to a Koszul-regular closed subscheme

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, affine dual Koszul calculation and localization.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- On the closed subscheme, the pullback of scalar Ext is the locally ranked
conormal-dual determinant. This makes no assertion about reconstructing a sheaf
on the ambient scheme from its pullback.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, proof of Lemma 48.15.5.
(blueprint: lem-sc-koszul-regular-immersion-ext-pullback).

Proof: Around z choose U = Spec A with ideal I generated by the supplied
Koszul-regular sequence f of length n. The closed immersion identifies its
preimage with Spec(A/I). The Koszul augmentation resolves A/I by finite free
A-modules, so bounded finite free Hom computes the restriction of derived Hom
into O_U. Sheafification is exact and sheaf Hom of finite free associated
modules is associated module Hom. Extending the Koszul complex to integer
cochain degrees gives the dual Koszul complex of the affine comparison lemma.
Its cohomology is zero except in degree n, where it is the restriction of the
A/I-module exterior^n Hom_{A/I}(I/I^2,A/I). Pullback of this cohomology sheaf
along Spec(A/I) -> Spec A tensors it with A/I; it is already an A/I-module,
so this tensor operation is canonically the identity. This is pullback AFTER
taking cohomology, not derived base change or pullback of the resolution.
The affine conormal frame identifies i^*I with the sheaf of I/I^2 and identifies
its stalk rank with n. Thus hr makes r identically n on this preimage.
If q = n the displayed pullback is the top exterior sheaf, and otherwise it is
zero. This is exactly locallyRankedExteriorTerm, since the rank-q open is
clopen. The normalized dual Koszul comparison is independent of generators
and commutes with localization. Hence on any intersection of charts the local
maps agree after refinement by affine standard opens, even without an affine
intersection or quasi-separatedness assumption. Their inverses agree too.
The sheaf condition glues both directions to an O_Z-linear isomorphism.
There is no ambient-support reconstruction in this argument. For n = 0 the
empty Koszul sequence gives O_Z in degree zero and zero elsewhere; an empty
source or an empty rank stratum gives zero. No Noetherian or global rank bound
is used. Chart calculations can be performed in the standard derived universe
and compared to the given one using the common K-injective Hom complex. -/
theorem koszulRegularImmersion_ext_pullback
    {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace))]
    (hregular : ∀ z : Z, ∃ U : Y.affineOpens, i z ∈ U.1 ∧
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → Γ(Y, U.1)),
        Ideal.span (Set.range f) = i.ker.ideal U ∧
          RingTheory.Sequence.IsKoszulRegular f)
    (r : LocallyConstant Z ℕ)
    (hr : ∀ z : Z, r z = Module.finrank (Z.presheaf.stalk z)
      ((RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor Z.toRingedSpace z).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback i).obj i.ker.toModules)))
    {q : ℤ} (hq : 0 ≤ q) :
    let F : Y.Modules := (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace)) q).obj
        ((derivedInternalHom (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y) Y.toRingedSpace.sheaf).obj
          (op ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
            (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace)) 0).obj
              ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj (SheafOfModules.unit Z.ringCatSheaf))),
            (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
              (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace)) 0).obj
                (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf)))
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback i).obj F ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.locallyRankedExteriorTerm
      (SheafOfModules.homObj (R := Z.sheaf)
        ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback i).obj i.ker.toModules)
        (SheafOfModules.unit Z.ringCatSheaf)) r q)) := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
